OL,4,T7#####################################k
OL,5,T5FKHASBULATOV FREED UNDER AMNESTY    Tj
OL,6,T5GPresident Boris Yeltsin's bitterestTj
OL,7,T5Gpolitical foes, Ruslan Khasbulatov Tj
OL,8,T5Gand Alexander Rutskoi, have both   Tj
OL,9,T5Gbeen freed from jail.              Tj
OL,10,T5F                                   Tj
OL,11,T5FEx-parliament chairman Khasbulatov Tj
OL,12,T5Fand ex-vice president Rutskoi were Tj
OL,13,T5Ffreed in line with the amnesty     Tj
OL,14,T5Fpassed by parliament for the       Tj
OL,15,T5Fplotters of last year's failed coupTj
OL,16,T5F                                   Tj
OL,17,T5FThree more of Mr Yeltsin's most    Tj
OL,18,T5Fsenior enemies, including the army Tj
OL,19,T5Fgeneral who led an attack on       Tj
OL,20,T5FMoscow's Ostankino TV centre duringTj
OL,21,T5Fthe uprising, have also been freed.Tj
